<title>UK: Ashquay to develop 20 mln stg Welsh site.</title>
<headline>Ashquay to develop 20 mln stg Welsh site.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>British property developer Ashquay Group Plc said on Monday it had agreed with Whitbread Developments and a local landowner a 20 million stg industrial development scheme in Magor, South Wales.</p>
<p>It said Taylor Woodrow Construction had been chosen as preferred contractor.</p>
<p>The scheme is two miles from the new crossing for the Severn River, which divides South Wales from England, and is next to the existing Whitbread brewery, Ashquay said in a statement.</p>
<p>The site covers some 17 acres and could form part of a larger, 48 acre site.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
